# VSIX allowlist (REFACTOR-PLAN §4.1, task 1.4): everything is ignored unless re-included
# below. vsce's negations override ignores, so what ships is exactly this list — when the
# extension starts loading a new file at runtime, add it here; anything forgotten stays out
# (and is caught by the manifest test in tests/distBuild.test.mjs) rather than leaking in.
**

# The dist pipeline's output (scripts/build/build.mjs): the host bundle, and the askpass
# launchers + helper git's credential prompts run (enumerated rather than !dist/askpass/** so a
# development build's source maps can never slip into a package). dist/automation/ (the
# --automation variant) is deliberately NOT re-included here: the default VSIX carries no
# automation code — the compile-time switch keeps it out of dist/extension.js, and this list
# keeps the variant's files out even when a previous local automation build left them in the
# tree. The automation VSIX run (scripts/automation-packaging.mjs) patches this file to swap
# the two.
!dist/extension.js
!dist/askpass/askpass.sh
!dist/askpass/askpass-empty.sh
!dist/askpass/askpassMain.js

# The webview bundle (scripts/build/webview.mjs output, kept at media/ this wave): the
# first-paint entry plus the on-demand chunks of task 5.9's code splitting (the entry reaches
# them through relative dynamic import(), so a missing chunk breaks the first open of its
# widget), and the vendored libraries the comparison pages load (scripts/package-highlight.js).
# Source maps are dev-only and stay out.
!media/out.min.js
!media/out.min.css
!media/chunks/*.js
!media/comparison.min.js
!media/comparison.min.css
!media/binaryCompare.min.js
!media/binaryCompare.min.css
!media/vendor/**

# Static assets: the marketplace icon, the command icons package.json contributes, the view
# icons gitGraphView.ts references, the data-loss-warning mascot and the notification logos.
# resources/automation/ (the in-page shim) ships only in the automation VSIX.
!resources/icon.png
!resources/git-graph-rs-cmd-icon-*.svg
!resources/git-graph-rs-webview-icon*.svg
!resources/feidudu.webp
!resources/notification/*.png

# Third-party license texts.
!licenses/**

# The prebuilt engine binaries, one per platform directory under native/ (the sources, build
# scripts and Cargo files above them stay out).
!native/**/git-graph.node

# The manifest (vsce force-includes package.json and README.md regardless) and the localized
# string tables the %...% placeholders resolve against.
!package.json
!package.nls.json
!package.nls.zh-cn.json
!LICENSE
